recon_accept
Usage: recon_accept

Accept the current machine as the recon baseline.

	recon_accept

Recon records what the hardware around the stick looks like and reports,
on every boot, any machine whose inventory has changed since its
baseline -- a new one it has never seen, or a known one that is not what
it was. That report keeps firing until a human decides the change is
expected. This is that decision: the reported inventory becomes the new
baseline, and the machine stops being flagged.

Run it only once you have looked at what changed and know why. It says
which machines it accepted; with nothing flagged it says there was
nothing to accept.

See also: lspci, lsusb, dmesg
